{
  "id": "modifier",
  "term": "modifier",
  "definition": "In this context, a modifier is a clinical qualifier used to indicate that loneliness is persistent, distressing, and important enough to affect a person’s psychiatric presentation, functioning, treatment involvement, prognosis, or recovery. It is based not just on severity, but also on the person’s developmental and cultural context, relationships, subjective meaning, consequences, and whether the disconnection is unwanted rather than a chosen or short-term solitude.",
